title: karr import --yes wipes the board when tasks/ exists but is empty
updated: 2026-08-10T01:27:58Z
---

`lib/App/karr/BoardStore.pm:312-314`, with the guard in `Cmd/Import.pm`.

The guard only checks that `tasks/` **exists**. An empty `tasks/` means "there
is no file view to import", but it takes the deletion path instead:

    karr materialize
    rm -f tasks/*.md
    karr import --yes
    -> Imported 0 task(s) ...    EXIT=0
    karr list -> 0 task(s)

The whole board is gone and the command reports success. This gets more likely
in combination with the materialize ticket: `tasks/` at repo root is a plausible
pre-existing project directory, and one that karr will happily empty.

Fix: treat an empty `tasks/` as "nothing to import" and refuse, or require an
explicit flag to mean "yes, import zero tasks and delete everything".
Fixed and merged into main; full suite green at 88 files / 566 tests.

Every one of these was reproduced before it was fixed and left a regression test
that was verified to fail against the pre-fix code -- not a test that merely
passes now. Details and what was deliberately NOT fixed are in the merge commit
that names this ticket.
